# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo and on checkout, regardless
# of the cloning machine's platform or local core.autocrlf setting --
# this is what actually fixes inconsistent line endings for good,
# rather than a one-off manual conversion that only holds until the
# next person with a different local git config touches the file (see
# the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning this was added to resolve).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for safety, even though Git's binary-detection heuristic
# would likely catch these anyway -- never attempt line-ending
# conversion on the PNG test/reference data in this repo.
*.png binary

# Explicit for the same reason as *.png above, even though the blanket
# `* text=auto eol=lf` rule already covers this -- definitions/*.json is
# regenerated by tools/extract_mercenary_skills.py, which itself now
# writes LF directly (newline="\n" on every output open()) specifically
# to avoid Windows' default CRLF translation. Making the LF requirement
# explicit here too means it holds even if that script's own newline
# handling ever regresses.
*.json text eol=lf
